<title>INDIA: Indian soybeans ease, processors' demand low.</title>
<headline>Indian soybeans ease, processors' demand low.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices eased in central Indian markets on limited demand from processing plants. Prices were decreased by 100-150 rupees per tonne today. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was down by 200 rupees per tonne on increased selling by solvent plants against limited buying by vanaspati units. Soyoil refined was steady but undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were better on reports of buoyancy in international prices. Soymeal yellow was $322-323 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $121-122 per tonne FAS in bulk for export and was 4,200 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was strong.</p>
